      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To navigate a roof insurance claim in Utah successfully, get an independent professional inspection before calling your insurance company."
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Opinions on\nReddit\nare mixed regarding whether you should let a roofing company file on your behalf; many users advise caution and suggest working directly with your insurer while having a trusted contractor present.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Reddit",
            "link": "https://www.reddit.com/r/Utah/comments/1jk2w05/roofer_wants_to_file_a_claim_in_our_behalf_to_our/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step-by-Step Claim Process"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check your policy: Look at your deductible and confirm whether you have Replacement Cost Value (RCV) or Actual Cash Value (ACV) coverage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document damage: Take clear photos of missing shingles, dented flashing, and granule loss, and note the date the storm or damage happened."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an independent inspection: Hire a reputable local roofer to evaluate the roof before filing so you know if the damage exceeds your deductible."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File the claim: Contact your insurance carrier with your policy number, photos, and the date of the storm."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the adjuster: Ask your chosen local roofing contractor to be on-site during the insurance adjuster's inspection to ensure no damage is missed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review scope and payouts: Review the first check (usually ACV minus your deductible) and request supplements if the initial estimate misses required repairs or local building codes."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Complete repairs and release depreciation: Finish the build with your contractor, submit the completion invoice, and receive your final depreciation check."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Consult official resources like the\nUtah Insurance Department\nfor general homeowner claim guidelines.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like more tailored help, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of damage\noccurred (hail, heavy snow, wind)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you know if your policy is RCV or ACV?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
